{
  "mark.2.p1.b1": {
    "text": "A few days later Jesus went back to Capernaum. And when the people heard that He was home,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p1.b2": {
    "text": "They gathered in such large numbers that there was no more room, not even outside the door,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p1.b3": {
    "text": "As Jesus spoke the word to them.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p1.b4": {
    "text": "Then a paralytic was brought to Him, carried by four men.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p2.b1": {
    "text": "Since they were unable to get to Jesus through the crowd,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p2.b2": {
    "text": "They uncovered the roof above Him, made an opening,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p2.b3": {
    "text": "And lowered the paralytic on his mat.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p2.b4": {
    "text": "When Jesus saw their faith,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p2.b5": {
    "text": "He said to the paralytic,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p2.b6": {
    "text": "Son, your sins are forgiven.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p3.b1": {
    "text": "But some of the scribes were sitting there and thinking in their hearts,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p3.b2": {
    "text": "Why does this man speak like this?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p3.b3": {
    "text": "He is blaspheming!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p3.b4": {
    "text": "Who can forgive sins but God alone?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p3.b5": {
    "text": "At once Jesus knew in His spirit that they were thinking this way within themselves. … He asked.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p3.b6": {
    "text": "Why are you thinking these things in your hearts?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p3.b7": {
    "text": "To say to a paralytic, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:9"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p3.b8": {
    "text": "Which is easier: … or to say, ‘Get up, pick up your mat, and walk’?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:9"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p4.b1": {
    "text": "But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins...",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p4.b2": {
    "text": "He said to the paralytic,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p4.b3": {
    "text": "I tell you, get up, pick up your mat, and go home.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p4.b4": {
    "text": "And immediately the man got up, picked up his mat,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p4.b5": {
    "text": "And walked out in front of them all.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p4.b6": {
    "text": "As a result, they were all astounded and glorified God, saying,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p4.b7": {
    "text": "We have never seen anything like this!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p5.b1": {
    "text": "As He was walking along, He saw Levi son of Alphaeus sitting at the tax booth.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p5.b2": {
    "text": "Follow Me,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p5.b3": {
    "text": "And Levi got up and followed Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p6.b1": {
    "text": "While Jesus was dining at Levi’s house, many tax collectors and sinners were eating with Him and His disciples",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p6.b2": {
    "text": "When the scribes who were Pharisees saw Jesus eating with these people,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p7.b1": {
    "text": "Why does He eat with tax collectors and sinners?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p7.b2": {
    "text": "It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p7.b3": {
    "text": "I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p8.b1": {
    "text": "Now John’s disciples and the Pharisees were often fasting.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p8.b2": {
    "text": "John’s disciples and those of the Pharisees",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p8.b3": {
    "text": "Why don’t Your disciples fast…?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p9.b1": {
    "text": "How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while He is with them?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:19"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p9.b2": {
    "text": "But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them;",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p9.b3": {
    "text": "Then they will fast.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p10.b1": {
    "text": "No one sews a patch of unshrunk cloth on an old garment. … a worse tear will result.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p10.b2": {
    "text": "And no one pours new wine into old wineskins. … both the wine and the wineskins will be ruined.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p10.b3": {
    "text": "Instead, new wine is poured into new wineskins.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p11.b1": {
    "text": "One Sabbath Jesus was passing through the grainfields,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p11.b2": {
    "text": "Look, why are they doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p12.b1": {
    "text": "Have you never read what David did when he and his companions were hungry and in need?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:25"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p12.b2": {
    "text": "He entered the house of God and ate the consecrated bread,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p12.b3": {
    "text": "And he gave some to his companions as well.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p12.b4": {
    "text": "Which was lawful only for the priests.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p13.b1": {
    "text": "The Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.2.p13.b2": {
    "text": "Therefore, the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 2:28"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  }
}
